[
  "Shot with a Canon EOS R5, 85mm f/1.8 lens. The composition features two shallow, matte ceramic bowls set on an aged, dark oak tabletop, centered to allow for circular cropping. Camera angle is a 3/4 overhead view, capturing the full depth of the bowls. Depth of field is shallow, with the front bowl in sharp focus and the second bowl slightly blurred behind. Lighting is soft, natural side light from a window on the left, creating gentle, realistic shadows and highlighting the texture of the fruit. The setting includes a rumpled linen napkin tucked beside the bowls and a few scattered, roughly chopped bright green pistachios on the wood surface. Inside each bowl, a smooth, thick layer of creamy white Greek yogurt serves as the base. Two tender, pearly-off-white poached pear halves are nestled into the yogurt, showing delicate, soft edges from the poaching process. A piece of curled orange peel and a small fragment of cinnamon stick are placed artfully near the pears for color contrast. The dish is finished with a generous sprinkle of vivid green chopped pistachios over the top. The overall color palette is warm, featuring earthy browns, creamy whites, and bright pops of herb green. Photorealistic, not AI-generated looking. The scene should look like someone just finished cooking and plating — lived-in, warm, authentic. Slight natural imperfections: an asymmetric placement of the pears, a small smudge of yogurt on the bowl rim, and a stray grain of spice. No plastic sheen, no unnaturally smooth surfaces, no perfect symmetry. Warm, golden-hour color temperature — cozy and inviting, not cold or clinical. No text, no watermark, no logo, no hands, no faces. Indistinguishable from a professional cookbook photograph."
]
